{
  "_doc": "Spec for every 3D model in the office and factory (docs/WORLDS_3D_MODEL_LIST.md). glTF axes: +Y up, metres; `facing` is the axis the front points along. Furniture is fitted by the app (height_m, then footprint), so sizes are checked loosely; materials and orientation are checked strictly. `palette` is only used to sort a generated model's faces into material slots. `materials` = names the app accepts; `classify` = the slots clean_model.py sorts faces into. Files whose sha256 is in `legacy_sha256` are the shipped Kenney kit (runtime-fitted, 28-200 triangles): reported, not failed.",
